    "atom::42a8d7d145acafeefeb67e2a": {
      "atom_id": "atom::42a8d7d145acafeefeb67e2a",
      "source_handle": "P0220",
      "field_path": [
        "study_summary_A",
        "problem_or_question"
      ],
      "value": "旨在解决肠道微生物代谢物在癌症发生发展及治疗响应中扮演的复杂角色尚不明确的问题，特别是其双重/矛盾功能及具体分子机制。目的是为未来科学研究提供新思路，并探索利用代谢物改善癌症治疗的潜在策略。",
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::c74ceafaf0f44d4428d1f44c9834e5d308c0933c5efca4ee53b7106017abb26b",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "problem_or_question"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::0bea90acc407fb27052be88d49df9c0eb4e8c864575fcfb5ebb2014addf9d2da",
      "multiple_values_in_field": false
    },
    "atom::7aa315b711ede69909f5c8d2": {
      "atom_id": "atom::7aa315b711ede69909f5c8d2",
      "source_handle": "P0220",
      "field_path": [
        "study_summary_A",
        "research_scope"
      ],
      "value": "肠道微生物群衍生的代谢物（Gut microbiota-derived metabolites）在肿瘤进展（Tumor Progression）和癌症治疗（Cancer Therapy）中的作用。涵盖多种癌症类型（如结肠癌、肝癌、乳腺癌等），重点讨论代谢物对肿瘤微环境（TME）、信号通路及免疫细胞的影响，以及其在放化疗和免疫治疗中的调节作用。",
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::c74ceafaf0f44d4428d1f44c9834e5d308c0933c5efca4ee53b7106017abb26b",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "research_scope"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::a42fbd908169ab25e7b5f94ef8bf6200cc58d34dfb1cbc37951dd64cf757180c",
      "multiple_values_in_field": false
    },
    "atom::8050b9f4e149b36a2ef8c37c": {
      "atom_id": "atom::8050b9f4e149b36a2ef8c37c",
      "source_handle": "P0220",
      "field_path": [
        "study_summary_A",
        "work_summary"
      ],
      "value": "该综述系统总结了肠道微生物代谢物与癌症之间的关联。首先阐述了代谢物如何通过重塑肿瘤微环境和调节关键信号通路（如MAPK, PI3K/Akt, NFκB, Wnt）来影响肿瘤进展，既包括促癌作用也包括抑癌作用。其次，分析了代谢物如何调节化疗药物（如伊立替康、吉西他滨）的疗效和毒性，以及如何增强或削弱免疫检查点阻断疗法（ICB）的效果。文章特别指出了部分代谢物（如短链脂肪酸SCFAs、石胆酸LCA、肌苷Inosine）具有情境依赖性的矛盾功能（Paradoxical Functions）。最后，综述了基于代谢物的新型治疗策略，包括饮食干预、噬菌体疗法、粪菌移植（FMT）、合成生物学改造及益生菌/益生元应用。",
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::c74ceafaf0f44d4428d1f44c9834e5d308c0933c5efca4ee53b7106017abb26b",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "work_summary"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::f8e5eba51d4f41b84a0216e7cba6993ba980cbfcbdd0cddac64833d713910cee",
      "multiple_values_in_field": false
    },
    "atom::0d513eb6cff96cd4c9bec6bf": {
      "atom_id": "atom::0d513eb6cff96cd4c9bec6bf",
      "source_handle": "P0220",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "planning_summary"
      ],
      "value": "该综述为理解肠道微生物如何通过代谢物调节免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）在实体瘤中的疗效提供了丰富的机制素材和背景信息。它详细列举了促进ICI疗效（如SCFAs、肌苷、MDP）和阻碍ICI疗效（如SCFAs在某些情况下、吲哚类代谢物）的具体代谢物及其作用路径，并讨论了克服耐药性的策略（如FMT）。此外，它还涵盖了代谢物对化疗药物代谢的影响，可作为对比或补充材料。",
      "role": "planner_interpretation",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::c74ceafaf0f44d4428d1f44c9834e5d308c0933c5efca4ee53b7106017abb26b",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "planning_summary"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::c3d21a4ce5a8b90cd92e1a442279fe3baf3f0d39265d018ebbf809ef9d8486f0",
      "multiple_values_in_field": false
    },
    "atom::6798a44a963a8960414fb94a": {
      "atom_id": "atom::6798a44a963a8960414fb94a",
      "source_handle": "P0220",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "facet_contributions"
      ],
      "value": {
        "boundaries": "主要基于已发表的观察性研究和部分机制研究，部分关联（如SCFAs与ICI响应的统计相关性）的详细机制仍需进一步阐明。不同癌症类型中代谢物的作用可能不同，需注意适用范围。",
        "contribution": "提供了微生物代谢物调节ICI疗效的具体实例和方向。例如，指出接受抗PD-1治疗的响应者体内SCFAs水平较高；肌苷在特定条件下增强抗CTLA-4和抗PD-1抗体疗效；Enterococcus肽聚糖产物MDP通过NOD2激活NFκB增强抗肿瘤能力；TMAO增强胰腺癌对ICB的反应。同时也提到了SCFAs可能在转移性黑色素瘤中限制抗CTLA-4抗体功能的反面证据。",
        "facet_id": "F1"
      },
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::c74ceafaf0f44d4428d1f44c9834e5d308c0933c5efca4ee53b7106017abb26b",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions",
            "0"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::ad98301dcab1fd048e17002e3c8ac3d548c95a285dc194b83a6f8ad08bb5361a",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::fca285e8c6539949bc6b753f": {
      "atom_id": "atom::fca285e8c6539949bc6b753f",
      "source_handle": "P0220",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "facet_contributions",
        "possible_uses"
      ],
      "value": "用于回答“肠道微生物如何调节ICI疗效”这一问题，提供具体的代谢物-免疫细胞互作案例，支持微生物组对ICI响应率影响的论点。",
      "role": "planning",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::c74ceafaf0f44d4428d1f44c9834e5d308c0933c5efca4ee53b7106017abb26b",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions",
            "0",
            "possible_uses"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::ba676e4f04128e9f5df40caa9be6bb5309e2409716c913f6281b4ce3d3a38a9e",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::723d64302b82cfc9ce8e48f3": {
      "atom_id": "atom::723d64302b82cfc9ce8e48f3",
      "source_handle": "P0220",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "facet_contributions"
      ],
      "value": {
        "boundaries": "机制描述多基于体外细胞实验或动物模型（如小鼠），直接外推到人体需谨慎。部分机制（如TMAO的具体通路）仍被作者标记为“未完全阐明”。",
        "contribution": "详细描述了代谢物介导ICI疗效的分子机制。包括：1. SCFAs通过抑制HDAC、调节mTOR活性增强T细胞功能；2. 肌苷通过A2AR-cAMP-PKA通路促进Th1分化，并抑制UBA6稳定MHC I和PD-L1；3. MDP通过NOD2-NFκB通路激活巨噬细胞和T细胞；4. 吲哚类代谢物通过AhR抑制TAMs功能从而抑制CD8+ T细胞；5. FMT通过改变血清次级胆汁酸水平克服耐药。",
        "facet_id": "F2"
      },
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::c74ceafaf0f44d4428d1f44c9834e5d308c0933c5efca4ee53b7106017abb26b",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions",
            "1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::ad98301dcab1fd048e17002e3c8ac3d548c95a285dc194b83a6f8ad08bb5361a",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::0749e786a5d5d2f6a0cfa32a": {
      "atom_id": "atom::0749e786a5d5d2f6a0cfa32a",
      "source_handle": "P0220",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "facet_contributions",
        "possible_uses"
      ],
      "value": "用于回答“哪些机制介导了这种效应”，提供从受体结合、信号转导到基因表达调控的多层次机制解释。",
      "role": "planning",
      "origins": [
